{
  "title": "Second conjugation: present tense",
  "note": "Second-conjugation verbs end in -ere with a long e (videre, to see) and keep that e in every present form: video, vides, videt, videmus, videtis, vident. Many verbs take an infinitive: Debeo laborare, I ought to work. Valere (to be well) gives the farewell vale.",
  "src": { "t": "Allen and Greenough, Verb Conjugations", "u": "https://dcc.dickinson.edu/grammar/latin/verb-conjugations" },
  "items": [
